	(text "HOST INTERFACE AND SUPPLY"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c4727c8c-1c36-5815-8725-290100ae5363")
	)
	(text "Host rail 3.3 V nominal (3.0-3.6 V).  EN high for one reading: wait 3.5 ms (LDO start 2.8 ms max),\ntime 64 periods of FOUT, sample REF - AMP, then EN low.  About 25 mA while on."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d9801d65-62ae-5714-87d8-f86e15a96289")
	)
	(text "OSCILLATOR  129 MHz in air, 81 MHz in water"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 102.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b5358843-fd89-5c16-a0f7-a5560f090dd5")
	)
	(text "Cross-coupled pair across a parallel tank: L1 + L2, C4 and the probe strips E1.\nR3 in series with C4 makes tank loss rise as f^2.  The strips are a quarter wave long\nat 160-600 MHz, which gives the tank a second resonance; without R3 the pair hops to it\nin water and saturated soil.  With R3 that mode is at least twice as lossy as the wanted one.\nR4, R5 damp a GHz emitter-follower mode through the SOT-23 lead inductance.\nSimulated minimum is 10 R; their delay sets the loss pulling, so keep 22 R.\nE1: two 5.5 mm strips 7 mm apart, 86 mm long, on In1.Cu and In2.Cu (copper zones)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 236.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ffcc3c29-5572-5dd4-8d04-2a0f5f09560f")
	)
	(text "LOSS DETECTOR AND SOIL TEMPERATURE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 252.73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3d21cf04-5464-5aee-91f9-c85e63ad116e")
	)
	(text "VE rides up with oscillation amplitude.  Q3 is the same transistor at half the tail current, no RF.\nREF - AMP: 0 when stalled, about 40 mV in air, falling as probe loss rises.  TH1 reads against a host pull-up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 282.702 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0ba93eca-be12-5291-a289-57522b665d2a")
	)
	(text "SQUARER AND /1024 PRESCALER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170.18 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "db62a18a-9d2e-5f93-be44-53ae38df6e97")
	)
	(text "FOUT = f_osc / 1024: 126 kHz in air, 79 kHz in water.\nR11, R12 isolate comparator kickback from the tank.\nU3 clocks at up to 140 MHz (160 MHz guaranteed).\nU5 needs /4 ahead of it (75 MHz guaranteed at 3.3 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170.18 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "45fd7f99-76c4-50f3-a2d4-257691e18eac")
	)
